# Complete Architecture: CA Assist Chatbot (Hybrid Model)

Based on your system specifications (8GB RAM, Intel HD Graphics with 128MB VRAM), building a 100% local AI will freeze your computer. Therefore, we are proceeding with the **Hybrid Architecture**. This gives you the speed and intelligence of a massive supercomputer, while keeping all your documents stored locally on your own hard drive.

## System Architecture Diagram

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Your Laptop (Localhost)"
        UI[React Frontend UI]
        API[FastAPI Backend Server]
        EMB[Local Embedding Model\nall-MiniLM-L6-v2]
        DB[(ChromaDB\nLocal Vector Store)]
        
        UI <-->|User Chat & UI| API
        API -->|1. Upload Document| EMB
        EMB -->|2. Store Vectors| DB
        API -->|3. Search Vectors| DB
    end

    subgraph "The Cloud (Free API)"
        GROQ[Groq Cloud API\nLlama-3 70B Model]
    end

    API <-->|4. Send Prompt + Found Context\nReceive Streamed Answer| GROQ
```

## The 5 Core Components

### 1. Frontend (The Face)
- **Tech:** React, Vite, Vanilla CSS.
- **What it does:** This is the beautiful, dark-mode UI we already built. It handles the user interface, chat bubbles, and document uploads.

### 2. Backend Server (The Brain's Manager)
- **Tech:** Python, FastAPI.
- **What it does:** Runs locally on your PC. It receives messages from the frontend, searches the database for relevant CA rules, and talks to the Cloud AI to get the final answer.

### 3. Vector Database (The Filing Cabinet)
- **Tech:** ChromaDB (Running locally).
- **What it does:** When you upload Income Tax Acts or Audit Manuals, this database stores them on your local hard drive. It uses a tiny amount of RAM (perfect for your 8GB PC) and allows the system to instantly search through thousands of pages of tax laws.

### 4. Embedding Model (The Translator)
- **Tech:** HuggingFace `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`.
- **What it does:** Runs locally. It translates your English text into mathematical numbers (vectors) so the Vector Database can search them. It is extremely small and won't slow down your PC.

### 5. Large Language Model (The Brain)
- **Tech:** Groq API (Running Llama-3 70B).
- **What it does:** This is the only part that doesn't run on your laptop. Because your laptop lacks a dedicated GPU, we use Groq's free cloud computers. When you ask a question, your local server sends the question + the relevant tax rules to Groq. Groq reads it, formulates a perfect CA-level answer in milliseconds, and sends it back to your screen.

